{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1363982-houserules-streamlining-combat-a-bit","id":1363982,"title":"Houserules: Streamlining combat a bit","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-01-29T09:43:53-08:00","id":1363982,"title":"Houserules: Streamlining combat a bit","content":"After a few months of actual, RAW play, here are the houserules I'm looking at using-- do they look good? Will they explode the game too much?<br /> <br /> <u><b>Combat: Quicker and Easier</b></u><ul><li><i><b>Turn Order will be fixed</b>, based on the initial Join Battle roll. Partially for the sake of my own sanity (even with a player taking over Ini tracking, it's still a pain that gets dramatically worse with more characters in play), and largely to prevent the doom spiral that comes from enemies acting quickly, getting withered down to low Ini, and having the party beat on them again before they get to recover. If you want to Clash, you can delay your action.</i><ul><li><b>Update</b>: after some testing, I'm downgrading this one a bit-- turn order gets recalculated at the start of each round, but initiative shifts during the round don't re-order things. That strikes a solid balance between unpredictability and book-keepeing.</li> </ul></li> <li><b>Soak will be retroactive</b>. Instead of reducing the <i>dice</i><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> of the damage roll by [Soak], the attacker rolls their full pool and you subtract </span><i>successes</i><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> equal to [half Soak, rounded up], to a minimum of the attacker's Overwhelm.</span></li> <li><i><b>Grapple will be single-roll</b>, based on Chausse's suggestion-- the gambit DC is the target's Strength, and if you succeed you get [Strength + Threshold successes] rounds of control. There's no immediate follow-up action; the target being hampered and restrained is enough of a result the first round.</i><ul><li><b>Update</b>: This one doesn't work so well; there are way too many Grapple charms that it messes with. Instead, I'm making the Initiative roll an auto-success and keeping everything else the same-- you roll to hit, pay 3 Ini, and make your Control roll. Have yet to see this one in action much, though.</li> </ul></li> <li><b>Combat Movement will be less reflexive, </b>because right now it's unintuitive as heck. A successful <b>Disengage moves you one range band</b> away without using your normal movement; a <b>Rush moves you one range band</b> without using your normal movement, but <b>those who beat your movement roll can immediately move back a band</b>.</li> </ul><br /> <u><b>NPCs: Less of a Headache</b></u><ul><li><b>No motes</b>-- all cost-restricted abilities will run off Willpower alone. That way I don't have to track individual pools.</li> <li><b>No number-boosting abilities</b>-- Charms and Merits that do nothing but boost rolls (ie, Rending Claw Slash) will be replaced by a bigger die pool. Having lots of dice tricks and situational tricks is fun for a player, but unnecessary complication for a GM.<ul><li>Except for sharply limited super-move type things (ie, Principle of Motion)</li> <li>Exalts will have a &quot;slow burn&quot; of ~3m/round worth of Excellencies factored into their die pools, with a full Excellency as a 1wp ability.</li> </ul></li> <li><b>Fewer Wound Penalties</b>-- If they have more than half their Health Levels remaining, they take no penalty; if they have less, they gain a -2 wound penalty. This is partially to simplify my life when it comes to tracking multiple foes, and partially to stave off the inevitable doom spiral a bit longer.</li> </ul><br /> <i>Updated 7/20/20 with to reflect more playtesting</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12314,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","user":"Grod_the_giant","date":". 07-20-2020, 11:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12314-grod_the_giant","name":"Grod_the_giant","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12314_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-29T10:17:16-08:00","id":1363986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grod_the_giant</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1363982-houserules-streamlining-combat-a-bit#post1363982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">After a few months of actual, RAW play, here are the houserules I'm looking at using-- do they look good? Will they explode the game too much?<br /> <br /> <u><b>Combat: Quicker and Easier</b></u><ul><li><b>Turn Order will be fixed</b>, based on the initial Join Battle roll. Partially for the sake of my own sanity (even with a player taking over Ini tracking, it's still a pain that gets dramatically worse with more characters in play), and largely to prevent the doom spiral that comes from enemies acting quickly, getting withered down to low Ini, and having the party beat on them again before they get to recover. If you want to Clash, you can delay your action.</li> <li><b>Soak will be retroactive</b>. Instead of reducing the <i>dice</i> of the damage roll by [Soak], the attacker rolls their full pool and you subtract <i>successes</i> equal to [half Soak, rounded up], to a minimum of the attacker's Overwhelm.</li> <li><b>Grapple will be single-roll</b>, based on Chausse's suggestion-- the gambit DC is the target's Strength, and if you succeed you get [Strength + Threshold successes] rounds of control. There's no immediate follow-up action; the target being hampered and restrained is enough of a result the first round.</li> <li><b>Combat Movement will be less reflexive, </b>because right now it's unintuitive as heck. A successful <b>Disengage moves you one range band</b> away without using your normal movement; a <b>Rush moves you one range band</b> without using your normal movement, but <b>those who beat your movement roll can immediately move back a band</b>.</li> </ul><u><b>NPCs: Less of a Headache</b></u><ul><li><b>No motes</b>-- all cost-restricted abilities will run off Willpower alone. That way I don't have to track individual pools.</li> <li><b>No number-boosting abilities</b>-- Charms and Merits that do nothing but boost rolls (ie, Rending Claw Slash) will be replaced by a bigger die pool. Having lots of dice tricks and situational tricks is fun for a player, but unnecessary complication for a GM.<ul><li>Except for sharply limited super-move type things (ie, Principle of Motion)</li> <li>Exalts will have a &quot;slow burn&quot; of ~3m/round worth of Excellencies factored into their die pools, with a full Excellency as a 1wp ability.</li> </ul></li> <li><b>Fewer Wound Penalties</b>-- If they have more than half their Health Levels remaining, they take no penalty; if they have less, they gain a -2 wound penalty. This is partially to simplify my life when it comes to tracking multiple foes, and partially to stave off the inevitable doom spiral a bit longer.</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>I really like (2) on Soak, it's a good idea. <br /> <br /> I'm happy you found (3) was a good idea, I think as well I will add the Strength to the rounds of Control, I think it's better.<br /> <br /> I did a personal subsystem in (5), but I think essentially your option is good enough when you have enough NPCs. Make them work like Fair Folk which have a big pool.<br /> <br /> (7) is definitely a good idea I didn't think of before. Thanks for the suggestion !","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}